## 3. Role-Based Authorization

| Requirement | Status | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| At least two roles defined | ✅ | [Admin](file:///c:/Users/eomis/CS392%20Project/CS392/Yummiez/Yummiez/Data/DbSeeder.cs#11-35) and [User](file:///c:/Users/eomis/CS392%20Project/CS392/Yummiez/Yummiez/Pages/Admin/Index.cshtml.cs#23-29) in [Constants/myRoles.cs](file:///c:/Users/eomis/CS392%20Project/CS392/Yummiez/Yummiez/Constants/myRoles.cs), seeded in [DbSeeder](file:///c:/Users/eomis/CS392%20Project/CS392/Yummiez/Yummiez/Data/DbSeeder.cs#9-85) |
| Role-based auth implemented | ⚠️ | Only on `TestRecords` and [Admin](file:///c:/Users/eomis/CS392%20Project/CS392/Yummiez/Yummiez/Data/DbSeeder.cs#11-35) pages |
| **ALL pages require authorization** | ❌ | [Restaurants](file:///c:/Users/eomis/CS392%20Project/CS392/Yummiez/Yummiez/Data/DbSeeder.cs#36-84) CRUD pages have **no** `[Authorize]` attribute |
| Pages restrict by role | ⚠️ | TestRecords: Create/Edit/Delete = Admin-only, Index/Details = any authenticated user. Restaurants: **no restrictions at all** |
| Access denied redirect | ✅ | Identity scaffolded [AccessDenied.cshtml](file:///c:/Users/eomis/CS392%20Project/CS392/Yummiez/Yummiez/Areas/Identity/Pages/Account/AccessDenied.cshtml) exists |

### What to Add

#### ❌ Add `[Authorize]` to ALL Restaurants pages:
- [Pages/Restaurants/Index.cshtml.cs](file:///c:/Users/eomis/CS392%20Project/CS392/Yummiez/Yummiez/Pages/Restaurants/Index.cshtml.cs) — `[Authorize]` (any authenticated user can view)
- [Pages/Restaurants/Details.cshtml.cs](file:///c:/Users/eomis/CS392%20Project/CS392/Yummiez/Yummiez/Pages/Restaurants/Details.cshtml.cs) — `[Authorize]` (any authenticated user)
- [Pages/Restaurants/Create.cshtml.cs](file:///c:/Users/eomis/CS392%20Project/CS392/Yummiez/Yummiez/Pages/Restaurants/Create.cshtml.cs) — `[Authorize(Roles = "Admin")]`
- [Pages/Restaurants/Edit.cshtml.cs](file:///c:/Users/eomis/CS392%20Project/CS392/Yummiez/Yummiez/Pages/Restaurants/Edit.cshtml.cs) — `[Authorize(Roles = "Admin")]`
- [Pages/Restaurants/Delete.cshtml.cs](file:///c:/Users/eomis/CS392%20Project/CS392/Yummiez/Yummiez/Pages/Restaurants/Delete.cshtml.cs) — `[Authorize(Roles = "Admin")]`

#### ⚠️ Consider global authorization:
You could add a global fallback authorization policy in [Program.cs](file:///c:/Users/eomis/CS392%20Project/CS392/Yummiez/Yummiez/Program.cs) so that **all** pages require auth by default (and then explicitly allow anonymous for Index/Privacy if desired):
```csharp
builder.Services.AddAuthorization(options =>
{
    options.FallbackPolicy = new AuthorizationPolicyBuilder()
        .RequireAuthenticatedUser()
        .Build();
});
```

#### ⚠️ Index and Privacy pages:
Your homepage ([Pages/Index.cshtml](file:///c:/Users/eomis/CS392%20Project/CS392/Yummiez/Yummiez/Pages/Index.cshtml)) and Privacy page currently have **no** `[Authorize]`. The milestone says "ALL application pages must require authorization." You need to either:
- Add `[Authorize]` to those pages, **or**
- Use the global fallback policy above and add `[AllowAnonymous]` only where justified (like the homepage).

